From 612dbf532a62f20cba19ecee439e003d9ef7a447 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:55:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] No silent partial results: pin every *_overflow_mode to throw

ClickHouse's overflow modes decide what a limit does: 'throw' fails the
query, 'break' (and 'any' for GROUP BY) returns what was read so far with
HTTP 200 and no marker. HyperDX set 'break' on metadata queries (filter
keys and values, the metric catalog, metric attribute values, MCP
previews), 'any' on value distributions and 'break' on raw SQL tables, and
passed a source's querySettings (charts, search, alerts) into the SQL
SETTINGS clause unfiltered, so a source or a server profile could make any
result partial. A short answer reads as a complete one.

- core/overflow.ts: NO_PARTIAL_RESULTS, the eleven overflow modes as
  'throw'.
- The client pins them last in processClickhouseSettings, over the call's
  own settings, on every query (charts, search, alerts, metadata, MCP).
- joinQuerySettings drops overflow modes from a source's querySettings (the
  SQL SETTINGS clause would override the pin).
- Limits stay; a query that reaches one fails and the UI shows the error.
  Removed the 'break'/'any' settings in metadata (getMapKeys x2,
  getMetadataMVKeyValues, getKeyValues, getValuesDistribution),
  useMetricCatalog, useFetchMetricAttributeValues, raw SQL tables
  (result_overflow_mode 'throw') and the MCP tools.
- One exception, a read sample for suggestion lists: getJSONKeys,
  getMapValues and the two text-index key/value lookups keep
  read_overflow_mode 'break' at max_rows_to_read through the new
  QueryInputs.allowSampledRead flag, which lets only the read modes
  through. Charts, search and alerts never set it.
